--- !u!114 &150576266
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 150576260}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ae309fc9b93c4434b888290b1d747f9a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TeacherInteraction
  playerMovement: {fileID: 0}
  teacherName: Nishiyama
  dialoguePopUp: {fileID: 1256853252}
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1682790333}
  spellSelectionScreen: {fileID: 0}
  battleScreen: {fileID: 0}
  element: 
  totalNumOfElementSpells: 0
  battleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  eventSystem: {fileID: 0}
  initalLines:
  - "Kon\u2019nichiwa! Hello and welcome in!"
  - "As long as you work hard, you\u2019ll be fluent in light magic in no time."
  - "In Japanese culture, among many folktales and festivals, there\u2019s one that\u2019s
    very closely related to the stars and light magic. This is the tale of Tanabata.
    There is a pair of lovers, Orihime the Weaver Princess and Hikoboshi the Cowherd."
  - "They are separated by the Milky Way which is like an impassable river. Once
    a year, on the night of Tanabata or the Japanese Star Festival, the lovers\u2019
    wish to be reunited comes true if there are clear skies. The magpies form a bridge
    for them."
  - "People make their own wishes on this night, writing their wishes on special
    papers called Tanzaku. Though it really doesn\u2019t matter what color paper
    you use, there are traditional meanings to each color."
  - "If you can understand them, it\u2019ll boost your light powers. Ganbatte!"
  afterPuzzleLines:
  - Did you notice that each Tanzaku had the image of a star on it?
  - Feel the light energy flowing through you even more!
  - "Let\u2019s have a discussion\u2014show me what you remember from the folktale
    I told you! Ikimashou!"
  afterBattleLines:
  - Subarashii! Excellent job.
  - "Your light shines brighter with every moment. You\u2019re ready for a new spell."
  afterSpellLines:
  - "Bring light to this world! Keep a positive attitude and you\u2019ll go very
    far!"
